hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"844","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abdillah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me, take from me; Allah has made for them a way: the previously married, one hundred lashes then stoning; and the virgin with the virgin, one hundred lashes and exile for a year."
"845","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, Zayd ibn Khalid, and Shibl, they said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man came and said: I adjure you by Allah, judge between us only by the Book of Allah. Then his opponent stood - and he was more understanding than him - and said: He spoke the truth; judge between us by the Book of Allah and permit me. He said: Speak. He said: My son was a laborer for this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. So I was told that upon my son is stoning, so I ransomed from him with one hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked men of knowledge, and they informed me that upon my son is one hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that upon the wife of this one is stoning. So he said: I shall judge between you two by the Book of Allah: the hundred sheep and the servant are returned; and upon your son is one hundred lashes and exile for a year; and go, O Unays, to the wife of this one - if she confesses, stone her. So she confessed, and he stoned her."
"846","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I feared that time would pass over people until one would say: We do not find stoning in the Book of Allah, and they would go astray by leaving an obligation Allah sent down. Verily stoning is true upon whoever commits adultery when married, when proof is established, or pregnancy, or confession. Verily the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and we stoned with him."
"847","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdillah (may Allah be pleased with them both): a man of Aslam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed to adultery before him; then he confessed and he turned away from him; then he confessed and he turned away from him, until he testified against himself four times. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you mad? He said: No. He said: Are you married? He said: Yes. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he was stoned at the prayer place. When the stones pained him, he fled. So he was caught and stoned until he died. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke good of him, and did not pray over him."
"848","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Samit, nephew of Abu Hurayrah, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: al-Aslami came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and testified against himself that he had approached a woman unlawfully four times, each time he turned away from him. Then he faced him the fifth time and said: Did you penetrate her? He said: Yes. He said: Until that of you disappeared in that of her, as the applicator disappears in the kohl container and the rope in the well? He said: Yes; I approached from her unlawfully what a man approaches from his wife lawfully. He said: What do you want by this statement? He said: I want you to purify me. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he was stoned. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard two men of his companions, one saying to his fellow: Look at this one whom Allah covered, but his soul did not leave him until he was stoned like a dog. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent to them. Then he traveled a while until he passed by the carcass of a donkey with its leg raised. So he said: Where are so-and-so and so-and-so? They said: We are these two, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Dismount and eat from the carcass of this donkey. They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah forgive you, who would eat from this? He said: What you just took from the honor of your brother is worse than eating carrion. By the One in whose hand is my soul, he is now in the rivers of Paradise, plunging therein."
"849","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him): a woman of Juhaynah confessed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to adultery. She said: I am pregnant. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well; when she delivers, inform me. So he did. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her, and her clothes were tied over her, then he ordered her stoning and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you stoned her then pray over her? So he said: She has repented a repentance that, had it been divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, would have encompassed them. Did you find better than that she gave herself to Allah?"
"850","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed us and said: O people, establish the prescribed penalties upon your slaves, those married of them and those unmarried. A slave-girl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed adultery, so he ordered me to flog her. So I came to her, and she was newly delivered of childbirth. So I feared that if I flogged her she would die - or he said: I would kill her - so I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. So he said: You did well."
"851","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf informed me that one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the Ansar informed him: a man of them complained until he wasted away, his skin upon his bone. Then a slave-girl of one of them entered, and he inclined to her and fell upon her. When men of his people entered upon him visiting him, he informed them of that and said: Seek a ruling for me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I fell upon a slave-girl who entered upon me. So they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen anyone among people in distress like his; were we to carry him to you, his bones would fall apart; he is but skin upon bone. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them a hundred stalks, and they struck him one strike."
"852","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Jurayj narrate from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man committed adultery, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he was flogged the penalty; then he was informed that he had been married, so he ordered him and he was stoned. Abu Muhammad said: Uthman ibn Umar, Abu Asim, and others narrated it, saying: A man committed adultery and was flogged, and they did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"853","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Maiz al-Aslami came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery. So he turned away from him, until he said that four times. So he said: Take him and stone him. So they went, and when he was stoned and felt the stones, he fled running. Then he passed a man with a camel's jawbone, who struck him and killed him. So they mentioned his flight to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he felt the stones. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not leave him?"
"854","al-Rabi ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."
"855","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the slave-girl when she commits adultery and is unmarried. So he said: If she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, sell her even for a rope. Ibn Shihab said: I do not know whether after the third or the fourth; and the rope is a cord."
"856","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jew and a Jewess."
"857","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Asbat - meaning Ibn Nasr - narrated to us, from Simak, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from his father Wail ibn Hujr, that a woman was fallen upon by a man in the darkness of dawn while she was heading to the mosque unwillingly, struggling against herself. So she sought help from a man who passed by her, and her assailant fled. Then a group of people passed by her, so she sought help from them, and they caught the one she had sought help from, while the other outran them and went. So they brought him leading him to her, and he said: I am only the one who helped you, and the other has gone. So they brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she informed him that he had fallen upon her, and the people informed him that they caught him running. So he said: I was helping her against her assailant, but these caught me and seized me. So she said: He lied; he is the one who fell upon me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him and stone him. He said: Then a man stood and said: Do not stone him, stone me; I am the one who did the deed to her - and he confessed. So three gathered before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the one who fell upon her, the one who helped her, and the woman. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, Allah has forgiven you. And he spoke good words to the one who helped her. Umar said: Stone the one who confessed adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, he has repented to Allah. Ibn Umayr said, adding in it: Had the people of Madinah - or the people of Yathrib - repented it, it would have been accepted from them. So he released them."
